From: Masatake YAMATO <yamato@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: shorten too long mcast group name

Upstream-commit: 73214f5d9f33b79918b1f7babddd5c8af28dd23d
Upstream: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/73214f5d9f33b79918b1f7babddd5c8af28dd23d

Backport the upstream one-line fix to the locked dior kernel. The old
16-character name fills name[GENL_NAMSIZ] without a NUL terminator;
modern libnl rejects the resulting multicast group name and aborts
the generic-netlink controller cache before nl80211 initialization.

Signed-off-by: Masatake YAMATO <yamato@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>
---
diff --git a/include/linux/thermal.h b/include/linux/thermal.h
index faf98fe5..e746571c 100644
--- a/include/linux/thermal.h
+++ b/include/linux/thermal.h
@@ -144,7 +144,7 @@ struct thermal_zone_device {
 /* Adding event notification support elements */
 #define THERMAL_GENL_FAMILY_NAME                "thermal_event"
 #define THERMAL_GENL_VERSION                    0x01
-#define THERMAL_GENL_MCAST_GROUP_NAME           "thermal_mc_group"
+#define THERMAL_GENL_MCAST_GROUP_NAME           "thermal_mc_grp"
 
 enum events {
 	THERMAL_AUX0,
